+# GR00T N1.7 OpenVINO Export
+
+This document describes the usage difference between these exporters:
+
+- `scripts/deployment/export_ov_n1d7.py`
+- `scripts/deployment/export_ov_n1d7_all_onnx.py`
+- `scripts/deployment/export_ov_n1d7_single_onnx_ov.py`
+- `scripts/deployment/export_ov_n1d7_single_ov.py`
+
+They support similar OpenVINO export workflows, but they use different conversion paths and are intended for different sharing and debugging workflows.
+
+## Which Script To Use
+
+### `export_ov_n1d7.py`
+
+Use this script when you want the shorter direct conversion path:
+
+- PyTorch -> OpenVINO IR
+
+This is the better choice when:
+
+- you are working inside this repository
+- you want the original direct-OV export path
+- you do not need a self-contained merged exporter script
+- you want to avoid the extra ONNX intermediate step
+
+### `export_ov_n1d7_all_onnx.py`
+
+Use this script when you want the fully merged single-file exporter:
+
+- PyTorch -> ONNX -> OpenVINO IR
+
+This is the better choice when:
+
+- you want one exporter file instead of several local helper scripts
+- you want all components to go through the same ONNX-based path
+- you want an easier script to share with another user
+- you want to debug ONNX artifacts as part of export
+
+### `export_ov_n1d7_single_onnx_ov.py`
+
+Use this script when you want one merged OpenVINO IR for the whole learned pipeline:
+
+- PyTorch -> ONNX -> one OpenVINO IR
+
+This is the better choice when:
+
+- you want to deploy one XML/BIN pair instead of several component models
+- you want one runtime call for ViT + LLM + VL self-attention + action head
+- you want a simpler parity check against one exported model directory
+- you are comfortable preparing `position_ids` and initial diffusion `actions` at runtime
+
+### `export_ov_n1d7_single_ov.py`
+
+Use this script when you want one merged OpenVINO IR for the whole learned pipeline, but with the direct OpenVINO conversion path:
+
+- PyTorch -> one OpenVINO IR
+
+This is the better choice when:
+
+- you want to deploy one XML/BIN pair instead of several component models
+- you want one runtime call for ViT + LLM + VL self-attention + action head
+- you want the single-IR direct-OV path instead of the ONNX-intermediate path
+- you want to keep the same single-IR CLI shape as `export_ov_n1d7_single_onnx_ov.py`
+
+## What This Script Does
+
+The first two scripts support these export modes:
+
+- `dit_only`: export only the DiT
+- `action_head`: export state encoder + action encoder + DiT or fused DiT + action decoder
+- `full_pipeline`: export ViT + LLM + VL self-attention + action head
+
+Both scripts also support two capture modes:
+
+- with `--dataset-path`: capture model inputs from a real dataset sample
+- without `--dataset-path`: capture model inputs from a synthesized dummy observation
+
+`export_ov_n1d7_single_onnx_ov.py` and `export_ov_n1d7_single_ov.py` always export the merged full neural pipeline and do not use `--export-mode`.
+
+## Main Difference
+
+### `export_ov_n1d7.py`
+
+Conversion path:
+
+- PyTorch -> OpenVINO IR
+
+Characteristics:
+
+- stays on the original direct OpenVINO export implementation
+- still depends on local repository files such as `export_onnx_n1d7.py` and the `gr00t/` package
+- good when you are exporting inside the same repo environment
+
+### `export_ov_n1d7_all_onnx.py`
+
+Conversion path:
+
+- PyTorch -> ONNX -> OpenVINO IR
+
+Characteristics:
+
+- merges logic that was previously split across multiple deployment helper scripts
+- keeps the `all_onnx` style CLI while removing local helper-script imports
+- useful when you want ONNX files and ONNX-based debugging during export
+
+### `export_ov_n1d7_single_onnx_ov.py`
+
+Conversion path:
+
+- PyTorch -> ONNX -> single OpenVINO IR
+
+Characteristics:
+
+- exports one merged wrapper instead of separate ViT, LLM, VL self-attention, and action-head IRs
+- verifies against a single wrapper output during export
+- writes single-OV metadata describing fixed vision grid, sequence length, and denoising steps
+- keeps `position_ids` as a runtime input instead of baking them into the graph
+- expects the runtime to supply the initial diffusion trajectory through the `actions` input
+
+### `export_ov_n1d7_single_ov.py`
+
+Conversion path:
+
+- PyTorch -> single OpenVINO IR
+
+Characteristics:
+
+- exports one merged wrapper instead of separate ViT, LLM, VL self-attention, and action-head IRs
+- uses the direct OpenVINO conversion path from `export_ov_n1d7.py`
+- keeps the same overall single-IR usage pattern as `export_ov_n1d7_single_onnx_ov.py`
+- verifies against a single wrapper output during export
+- keeps `position_ids` as a runtime input instead of baking them into the graph
+- expects the runtime to supply the initial diffusion trajectory through the `actions` input
+
+The script is still not fully standalone from the whole repository because it depends on the `gr00t/` package and the model checkpoint files.
+
+## File Requirements
+
+### For `export_ov_n1d7.py`
+
+Share at least:
+
+- `scripts/deployment/export_ov_n1d7.py`
+- `scripts/deployment/export_onnx_n1d7.py`
+- `gr00t/`
+- `pyproject.toml`
+- the checkpoint directory
+
+### For `export_ov_n1d7_all_onnx.py`
+
+Share at least:
+
+- `scripts/deployment/export_ov_n1d7_all_onnx.py`
+- `gr00t/`
+- `pyproject.toml`
+- the checkpoint directory
+
+### For `export_ov_n1d7_single_onnx_ov.py`
+
+Share at least:
+
+- `scripts/deployment/export_ov_n1d7_single_onnx_ov.py`
+- `scripts/deployment/export_ov_n1d7_all_onnx.py`
+- `gr00t/`
+- `pyproject.toml`
+- the checkpoint directory
+
+### For `export_ov_n1d7_single_ov.py`
+
+Share at least:
+
+- `scripts/deployment/export_ov_n1d7_single_ov.py`
+- `scripts/deployment/export_ov_n1d7.py`
+- `gr00t/`
+- `pyproject.toml`
+- the checkpoint directory
+
+## Minimum Files To Share
+
+For another user to run this exporter, share at least:
+
+- `scripts/deployment/export_ov_n1d7_all_onnx.py`
+- `gr00t/`
+- `pyproject.toml`
+- the checkpoint directory, for example `checkpoints/GR00T-N1.7-3B`
+
+The target machine also needs the Python environment used by this repository.
+
+## Environment Setup
+
+From the repository root:
+
+```bash
+uv sync --all-extras
+```
+
+If `uv` is not available, use an existing environment where GR00T inference already works.
+
+## Example Commands
+
+Run from the repository root.
+
+### 1. `export_ov_n1d7.py`: Full Pipeline Export Without Dataset
+
+```bash
+python scripts/deployment/export_ov_n1d7.py \
+  --model-path checkpoints/GR00T-N1.7-3B \
+  --embodiment-tag REAL_G1 \
+  --output-dir ~/openvino_models/real_g1_full_direct \
+  --export-mode full_pipeline \
+  --precision fp16 \
+  --device cpu
+```
+
+### 2. `export_ov_n1d7_all_onnx.py`: Full Pipeline Export Without Dataset
+
+```bash
+python scripts/deployment/export_ov_n1d7_all_onnx.py \
+  --model-path checkpoints/GR00T-N1.7-3B \
+  --embodiment-tag REAL_G1 \
+  --output-dir ~/openvino_models/real_g1_full \
+  --export-mode full_pipeline \
+  --use-fused-dit \
+  --precision fp16 \
+  --device cpu
+```
+
+### 3. `export_ov_n1d7.py`: Full Pipeline Export With Dataset
+
+```bash
+python scripts/deployment/export_ov_n1d7.py \
+  --model-path checkpoints/GR00T-N1.7-3B \
+  --dataset-path demo_data/libero_demo \
+  --embodiment-tag LIBERO_PANDA \
+  --output-dir ~/openvino_models/libero_full_direct \
+  --export-mode full_pipeline \
+  --precision fp16 \
+  --device cpu
+```
+
+### 4. `export_ov_n1d7_all_onnx.py`: Full Pipeline Export With Dataset
+
+```bash
+python scripts/deployment/export_ov_n1d7_all_onnx.py \
+  --model-path checkpoints/GR00T-N1.7-3B \
+  --dataset-path demo_data/libero_demo \
+  --embodiment-tag LIBERO_PANDA \
+  --output-dir ~/openvino_models/libero_full \
+  --export-mode full_pipeline \
+  --use-fused-dit \
+  --precision fp16 \
+  --device cpu
+```
+
+### 5. `export_ov_n1d7.py`: Minimal DiT-Only Export
+
+```bash
+python scripts/deployment/export_ov_n1d7.py \
+  --model-path checkpoints/GR00T-N1.7-3B \
+  --embodiment-tag REAL_G1 \
+  --output-dir ~/openvino_models/real_g1_dit_direct \
+  --export-mode dit_only \
+  --precision fp16 \
+  --device cpu
+```
+
+### 6. `export_ov_n1d7_all_onnx.py`: Minimal DiT-Only Export
+
+```bash
+python scripts/deployment/export_ov_n1d7_all_onnx.py \
+  --model-path checkpoints/GR00T-N1.7-3B \
+  --embodiment-tag REAL_G1 \
+  --output-dir ~/openvino_models/real_g1_dit \
+  --export-mode dit_only \
+  --precision fp16 \
+  --device cpu
+```
+
+### 7. `export_ov_n1d7_single_onnx_ov.py`: Single-IR Export Without Dataset
+
+```bash
+python scripts/deployment/export_ov_n1d7_single_onnx_ov.py \
+  --model-path checkpoints/GR00T-N1.7-3B \
+  --embodiment-tag REAL_G1 \
+  --output-dir ~/openvino_models/real_g1_single_ov \
+  --precision fp16 \
+  --device cpu
+```
+
+### 8. `export_ov_n1d7_single_onnx_ov.py`: Single-IR Export With Dataset
+
+```bash
+python scripts/deployment/export_ov_n1d7_single_onnx_ov.py \
+  --model-path checkpoints/GR00T-N1.7-3B \
+  --dataset-path demo_data/libero_demo \
+  --embodiment-tag LIBERO_PANDA \
+  --output-dir ~/openvino_models/libero_single_ov \
+  --precision fp16 \
+  --device cpu
+```
+
+### 9. `export_ov_n1d7_single_ov.py`: Single-IR Export Without Dataset
+
+```bash
+python scripts/deployment/export_ov_n1d7_single_ov.py \
+  --model-path checkpoints/GR00T-N1.7-3B \
+  --embodiment-tag REAL_G1 \
+  --output-dir ~/openvino_models/real_g1_single_direct_ov \
+  --precision fp16 \
+  --device cpu
+```
+
+### 10. `export_ov_n1d7_single_ov.py`: Single-IR Export With Dataset
+
+```bash
+python scripts/deployment/export_ov_n1d7_single_ov.py \
+  --model-path checkpoints/GR00T-N1.7-3B \
+  --dataset-path demo_data/libero_demo \
+  --embodiment-tag LIBERO_PANDA \
+  --output-dir ~/openvino_models/libero_single_direct_ov \
+  --precision fp16 \
+  --device cpu
+```
+
+## Main Arguments
+
+- `--model-path`: local checkpoint directory
+- `--dataset-path`: optional dataset path; if omitted, dummy capture mode is used
+- `--embodiment-tag`: embodiment name such as `REAL_G1`, `LIBERO_PANDA`, `XDOF`
+- `--output-dir`: directory where `.xml`, `.bin`, `.onnx`, and metadata are written
+- `--export-mode`: `dit_only`, `action_head`, or `full_pipeline`
+- `--use-fused-dit`: export fused denoising loop when supported
+- `--precision`: `fp32` or `fp16`
+- `--device`: export device, usually `cpu` or `cuda`
+- `--num-inference-timesteps`: optional override for denoising steps during export
+
+For `export_ov_n1d7_single_onnx_ov.py`, the main arguments are:
+
+- `--model-path`: local checkpoint directory
+- `--dataset-path`: optional dataset path; if omitted, dummy capture mode is used
+- `--embodiment-tag`: embodiment name such as `REAL_G1` or `NEW_EMBODIMENT`
+- `--output-dir`: directory where the merged `.xml`, `.bin`, metadata, and ONNX files are written
+- `--output-name`: output file prefix, default `gr00t_n1d7_single`
+- `--precision`: `fp32` or `fp16`
+- `--batch-size`: export batch size, default `1`
+- `--num-inference-timesteps`: optional denoising-step override before export
+- `--device`: export device, usually `cpu`
+
+For `export_ov_n1d7_single_ov.py`, the main arguments are the same.
+
+The CLI shape is intentionally the same between `export_ov_n1d7_single_onnx_ov.py` and `export_ov_n1d7_single_ov.py`, so commands can be switched with minimal changes. The main difference is only the conversion path:
+
+- `export_ov_n1d7_single_onnx_ov.py`: PyTorch -> ONNX -> one OpenVINO IR
+- `export_ov_n1d7_single_ov.py`: PyTorch -> one OpenVINO IR
+
+## Expected Outputs
+
+The exporter writes model files under the output directory, for example:
+
+- `export_metadata.json`
+- `vit_fp16.xml` / `vit_fp16.bin`
+- `llm_fp16.xml` / `llm_fp16.bin`
+- `vl_self_attention_fp16.xml` / `vl_self_attention_fp16.bin`
+- `state_encoder_fp16.xml` / `state_encoder_fp16.bin`
+- `action_encoder_fp16.xml` / `action_encoder_fp16.bin`
+- `dit_fp16.xml` / `dit_fp16.bin`
+- `action_decoder_fp16.xml` / `action_decoder_fp16.bin`
+- or `dit_fused_fp16.xml` / `dit_fused_fp16.bin`
+
+Actual outputs depend on `--export-mode` and whether `--use-fused-dit` is enabled.
+
+For `export_ov_n1d7_all_onnx.py`, the output directory may also contain intermediate `.onnx` files.
+
+For `export_ov_n1d7_single_onnx_ov.py`, the output directory typically contains:
+
+- `gr00t_n1d7_single_fp16.xml` / `gr00t_n1d7_single_fp16.bin`
+- `gr00t_n1d7_single_fp16.onnx`
+- `gr00t_n1d7_single_fp16.onnx.data`
+- `gr00t_n1d7_single_metadata.json`
+
+For `export_ov_n1d7_single_ov.py`, the output directory typically contains:
+
+- `gr00t_n1d7_single_from_ov_fp16.xml` / `gr00t_n1d7_single_from_ov_fp16.bin`
+- `gr00t_n1d7_single_from_ov_metadata.json`
+
+## Notes
+
+- `fp16` controls OpenVINO weight compression during save.
+- If no dataset is available, dummy capture is used only to collect representative tensor shapes for export.
+- If a checkpoint contains multiple embodiments, pass `--embodiment-tag` explicitly.
+- `export_ov_n1d7.py` is the direct-OV path.
+- `export_ov_n1d7_all_onnx.py` is the ONNX-intermediate path.
+- The single exporter removes local helper-script imports, but it still depends on the main `gr00t/` Python package.
+- `export_ov_n1d7_single_onnx_ov.py` exports one merged learned pipeline, but runtime still has to prepare `position_ids` and the initial diffusion `actions` seed.
+- `export_ov_n1d7_single_ov.py` exports one merged learned pipeline through the direct OpenVINO path, but runtime still has to prepare `position_ids` and the initial diffusion `actions` seed.
+- The single-OV metadata file records the fixed vision grid and denoising-step count used during export.
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+- If export fails, try `--export-mode dit_only` first to narrow the failing component.
+- If embodiment auto-detection is ambiguous, pass `--embodiment-tag` explicitly.
+- If ONNX Runtime is not installed, verification will be skipped but export can still proceed.
+- If OpenVINO conversion is slow, keep export on `cpu` unless you specifically need `cuda` for the PyTorch side.
