@@ -0,0 +1,436 @@
+# GR00T N1.7 OpenVINO Inference
+
+This document describes the current OpenVINO inference entrypoints for GR00T N1.7.
+
+The main inference files are:
+
+- `scripts/deployment/ov_n1d7_forward.py` — generic OpenVINO inference backend
+- `scripts/deployment/run_base_ov_inference.py` — base model inference (no dataset required)
+- `scripts/deployment/run_base_single_ov_inference.py` — single-IR base model inference (no dataset required)
+- `scripts/deployment/run_aloha_full_ov_accelerated.py` — ALOHA-specific inference (requires dataset)
+
+## Common Backend: `ov_n1d7_forward.py`
+
+This is the generic OpenVINO inference backend shared by all entrypoints.
+
+It contains:
+
+- common CLI argument definitions
+- OpenVINO model loading
+- partial OpenVINO setup
+- full OpenVINO setup
+- FP32-forced full OpenVINO setup for Intel iGPU stability
+- timing collection and summary logic
+- generic dataset inference loop
+
+It is intended to be imported by the entrypoint scripts below.
+
+## Required Model Files
+
+Your OpenVINO model directory should contain these files for the selected precision.
+
+For full pipeline inference:
+
+- `vit_fp16.xml` or `vit_fp32.xml`
+- `llm_fp16.xml` or `llm_fp32.xml`
+- `vl_self_attention_fp16.xml` or `vl_self_attention_fp32.xml`
+- `state_encoder_fp16.xml` or `state_encoder_fp32.xml`
+
+For fused action head mode:
+
+- `dit_fused_fp16.xml` or `dit_fused_fp32.xml`
+
+For 4-component action head mode:
+
+- `action_encoder_fp16.xml` or `action_encoder_fp32.xml`
+- `dit_fp16.xml` or `dit_fp32.xml`
+- `action_decoder_fp16.xml` or `action_decoder_fp32.xml`
+
+If you pass `--use-fused-dit` but `dit_fused_*.xml` is missing, `ov_n1d7_forward.py` will automatically fall back to the 4-component path when the three non-fused action-head files are present.
+
+## Environment Setup
+
+From the repository root:
+
+```bash
+uv sync --all-extras
+```
+
+Or run inside an existing environment where GR00T inference already works.
+
+## Main Inference Modes
+
+### Partial OpenVINO
+
+This uses the partial OpenVINO path.
+
+- OpenVINO is used for the accelerated components
+- some parts still run in PyTorch
+
+Run this by omitting `--full-ov`.
+
+### Full OpenVINO
+
+This uses the full OpenVINO path.
+
+- ViT in OpenVINO
+- LLM in OpenVINO
+- VL self-attention in OpenVINO
+- action head in OpenVINO
+
+Run this with `--full-ov`.
+
+### Full OpenVINO FP32
+
+Use this when Intel iGPU full-precision stability matters more than speed.
+
+Run this with:
+
+- `--full-ov`
+- `--force-fp32`
+
+---
+
+## Base Model Inference: `run_base_ov_inference.py`
+
+This is the generic base model inference script. It works with any embodiment tag supported by the base checkpoint and does not require a dataset.
+
+It synthesizes dummy observations from the checkpoint's `processor_config.json` and `statistics.json`, making it suitable for:
+
+- benchmarking OpenVINO IR models on different devices
+- validating exported IR models without needing real data
+- quick sanity checks after export
+
+### Runtime Dependencies
+
+- `scripts/deployment/run_base_ov_inference.py`
+- `scripts/deployment/ov_n1d7_forward.py`
+- `gr00t/`
+- `pyproject.toml`
+- the GR00T checkpoint directory (with `processor_config.json` and `statistics.json`)
+- the OpenVINO model directory
+
+### Arguments
+
+- `--model-path`: local PyTorch checkpoint directory
+- `--ov-model-dir`: directory containing OpenVINO IR files
+- `--embodiment-tag`: embodiment tag such as `REAL_G1`
+- `--num-samples`: number of timed inference iterations (default: 10)
+- `--num-warmup`: number of warmup iterations (default: 5)
+- `--device`: OpenVINO device — `GPU`, `CPU`, `NPU`, or `AUTO`
+- `--use-fused-dit`: use fused DiT when available
+- `--full-ov`: enable full OpenVINO inference path
+- `--force-fp32`: force FP32 precision for GPU inference
+- `--language`: language instruction for dummy input (default: "Pick and place the object.")
+- `--image-size`: image size H W for dummy input (default: 224 224)
+
+### Example Commands
+
+Run from the repository root.
+
+#### Base Model on GPU (Direct-Path IR, 4-Component)
+
+```bash
+python scripts/deployment/run_base_ov_inference.py \
+  --model-path checkpoints/GR00T-N1.7-3B \
+  --ov-model-dir checkpoints/real_g1_full_direct \
+  --embodiment-tag REAL_G1 \
+  --num-samples 10 \
+  --device GPU \
+  --full-ov
+```
+
+#### Base Model on GPU (ONNX-Path IR, Fused DiT)
+
+```bash
+python scripts/deployment/run_base_ov_inference.py \
+  --model-path checkpoints/GR00T-N1.7-3B \
+  --ov-model-dir checkpoints/real_g1_full_onnx \
+  --embodiment-tag REAL_G1 \
+  --num-samples 10 \
+  --device GPU \
+  --full-ov \
+  --use-fused-dit
+```
+
+#### Base Model on CPU
+
+```bash
+python scripts/deployment/run_base_ov_inference.py \
+  --model-path checkpoints/GR00T-N1.7-3B \
+  --ov-model-dir checkpoints/real_g1_full_direct \
+  --embodiment-tag REAL_G1 \
+  --num-samples 5 \
+  --device CPU \
+  --full-ov
+```
+
+#### LIBERO Checkpoint (LIBERO_PANDA)
+
+Download the LIBERO fine-tuned checkpoint:
+
+```bash
+huggingface-cli download nvidia/GR00T-N1.7-LIBERO \
+  --include "libero_10/config.json" "libero_10/embodiment_id.json" \
+  "libero_10/model-*.safetensors" "libero_10/model.safetensors.index.json" \
+  "libero_10/processor_config.json" "libero_10/statistics.json" \
+  --local-dir checkpoints/GR00T-N1.7-LIBERO
+```
+
+Export OpenVINO IR models:
+
+```bash
+python scripts/deployment/export_ov_n1d7.py \
+  --model-path checkpoints/GR00T-N1.7-LIBERO/libero_10 \
+  --embodiment-tag LIBERO_PANDA \
+  --output-dir checkpoints/libero_full_direct \
+  --export-mode full_pipeline \
+  --precision fp16 \
+  --device cpu
+```
+
+Run inference:
+
+```bash
+python scripts/deployment/run_base_ov_inference.py \
+  --model-path checkpoints/GR00T-N1.7-LIBERO/libero_10 \
+  --ov-model-dir checkpoints/libero_full_direct \
+  --embodiment-tag LIBERO_PANDA \
+  --num-samples 10 \
+  --device GPU \
+  --full-ov
+```
+
+### Notes
+
+- Does not require a dataset; constructs valid dummy observations automatically
+- Reads `processor_config.json` to determine video/state/language keys
+- Reads `statistics.json` to determine per-key state dimensions
+- For eef state keys (containing rot6d), dummy values use a valid identity rotation
+
+---
+
+## Single-IR Base Inference: `run_base_single_ov_inference.py`
+
+This is the single-OV runtime for the merged IR exported by `export_ov_n1d7_single_ov.py`.
+
+It is intended for:
+
+- benchmarking the merged single-IR export on CPU, GPU, NPU, or AUTO
+- validating one exported XML against the original PyTorch model without a dataset
+- checking embodiment-specific parity for the merged export path
+
+Unlike `run_base_ov_inference.py`, this script does not load separate ViT, LLM, VL self-attention, or action-head component models. It resolves exactly one XML from `--ov-model-dir` and runs the whole learned pipeline in one OpenVINO call.
+
+### Runtime Dependencies
+
+- `scripts/deployment/run_base_single_ov_inference.py`
+- `gr00t/`
+- `pyproject.toml`
+- the GR00T checkpoint directory with `processor_config.json` and usually `statistics.json`
+- the single-OV model directory containing exactly one XML model
+
+### Arguments
+
+- `--model-path`: local PyTorch checkpoint directory
+- `--ov-model-dir`: directory containing exactly one single-OV XML model
+- `--embodiment-tag`: embodiment tag such as `REAL_G1` or `NEW_EMBODIMENT`
+- `--num-samples`: number of timed inference iterations
+- `--num-warmup`: number of warmup iterations
+- `--verify-pytorch`: run one parity check against the original PyTorch model before timing
+- `--device`: OpenVINO device — `GPU`, `CPU`, `NPU`, or `AUTO`
+- `--language`: language instruction for dummy input
+- `--image-size`: image size H W for dummy input
+- `--diffusion-seed`: fixed seed used to sample the initial denoising trajectory for both PyTorch verification and OV inference
+
+### Example Commands
+
+Run from the repository root.
+
+#### Single-OV Base Model on CPU
+
+```bash
+python scripts/deployment/run_base_single_ov_inference.py \
+  --model-path checkpoints/GR00T-N1.7-3B \
+  --ov-model-dir checkpoints/gr00t_n1d7_ov_g1 \
+  --embodiment-tag REAL_G1 \
+  --device CPU \
+  --verify-pytorch
+```
+
+#### Single-OV Base Model on GPU
+
+```bash
+python scripts/deployment/run_base_single_ov_inference.py \
+  --model-path checkpoints/GR00T-N1.7-3B \
+  --ov-model-dir checkpoints/gr00t_n1d7_ov_g1 \
+  --embodiment-tag REAL_G1 \
+  --device GPU \
+  --verify-pytorch
+```
+
+#### Single-OV ALOHA-Style Finetuned Checkpoint Verification
+
+```bash
+python scripts/deployment/run_base_single_ov_inference.py \
+  --model-path /path/to/aloha_finetuned_checkpoint \
+  --ov-model-dir /path/to/gr00t_n1d7_single_ov \
+  --embodiment-tag NEW_EMBODIMENT \
+  --device CPU \
+  --verify-pytorch \
+  --diffusion-seed 0
+```
+
+### Notes
+
+- Does not require a dataset; constructs valid dummy observations automatically
+- Resolves exactly one XML from `--ov-model-dir`; if there are zero or multiple XML files, the script raises an error
+- The runtime reconstructs `position_ids` and, during verification, can also reuse the runtime-captured PyTorch `position_ids`
+- The `actions` input to the single-OV model is the initial denoising trajectory, not a decoded robot action
+- `--verify-pytorch` is only meaningful when PyTorch and OV use the same checkpoint and the same `--diffusion-seed`
+- The script logs both full-tensor metrics and trimmed active-action metrics, because some embodiments use far fewer than the padded `132` action channels
+
+---
+
+## ALOHA Inference: `run_aloha_full_ov_accelerated.py`
+
+This is the ALOHA-specific runnable entrypoint.
+
+It contains only the ALOHA-specific parts:
+
+- camera selection
+- ALOHA modality config
+- task mapping loading
+- converting one dataset row into GR00T observation format
+
+This is the script you run for ALOHA inference.
+
+### Runtime Dependencies
+
+- `scripts/deployment/run_aloha_full_ov_accelerated.py`
+- `scripts/deployment/ov_n1d7_forward.py`
+- `gr00t/`
+- `pyproject.toml`
+- the GR00T checkpoint directory
+- the OpenVINO model directory
+- the target dataset directory
+
+### Arguments
+
+- `--model-path`: local PyTorch checkpoint directory
+- `--dataset-path`: dataset directory used for inference samples
+- `--ov-model-dir`: directory containing OpenVINO IR files
+- `--embodiment-tag`: embodiment tag such as `NEW_EMBODIMENT`
+- `--num-cameras`: ALOHA camera count, currently `1` or `4`
+- `--num-samples`: number of dataset episodes to time
+- `--device`: OpenVINO device, usually `GPU`, `CPU`, `NPU`, or `AUTO`
+- `--use-fused-dit`: use fused DiT when fused model files are available
+- `--full-ov`: enable full OpenVINO inference path
+- `--force-fp32`: force FP32 precision for full GPU inference
+
+### Example Commands
+
+Run from the repository root.
+
+#### ALOHA Full OpenVINO
+
+```bash
+python scripts/deployment/run_aloha_full_ov_accelerated.py \
+  --model-path /path/to/checkpoint \
+  --dataset-path /path/to/aloha_dataset \
+  --ov-model-dir /path/to/ov_models \
+  --embodiment-tag NEW_EMBODIMENT \
+  --num-cameras 4 \
+  --num-samples 10 \
+  --device GPU \
+  --full-ov
+```
+
+#### ALOHA Full OpenVINO With Fused DiT
+
+```bash
+python scripts/deployment/run_aloha_full_ov_accelerated.py \
+  --model-path /path/to/checkpoint \
+  --dataset-path /path/to/aloha_dataset \
+  --ov-model-dir /path/to/ov_models \
+  --embodiment-tag NEW_EMBODIMENT \
+  --num-cameras 4 \
+  --num-samples 10 \
+  --device GPU \
+  --full-ov \
+  --use-fused-dit
+```
+
+#### ALOHA Full OpenVINO FP32
+
+```bash
+python scripts/deployment/run_aloha_full_ov_accelerated.py \
+  --model-path /path/to/checkpoint \
+  --dataset-path /path/to/aloha_dataset \
+  --ov-model-dir /path/to/ov_models \
+  --embodiment-tag NEW_EMBODIMENT \
+  --num-cameras 4 \
+  --num-samples 10 \
+  --device GPU \
+  --full-ov \
+  --force-fp32
+```
+
+#### ALOHA Partial OpenVINO
+
+```bash
+python scripts/deployment/run_aloha_full_ov_accelerated.py \
+  --model-path /path/to/checkpoint \
+  --dataset-path /path/to/aloha_dataset \
+  --ov-model-dir /path/to/ov_models \
+  --embodiment-tag NEW_EMBODIMENT \
+  --num-cameras 4 \
+  --num-samples 10 \
+  --device GPU
+```
+
+#### Example From A Real ALOHA Setup
+
+```bash
+taskset -c 11 python run_aloha_full_ov_accelerated.py \
+  --model-path ~/yue/gr00t_env/checkpoints/aloha_finetuned_insert_4c_100000 \
+  --dataset-path ~/yue/dataset/lerobot_aloha_sim_insertion_4c/ \
+  --ov-model-dir ~/yue/gr00t_env/model/tmp_fused_aloha_4c_insert_fp16_v3 \
+  --embodiment-tag NEW_EMBODIMENT \
+  --num-samples 4 \
+  --num-cameras 4 \
+  --device GPU \
+  --full-ov
+```
+
+If `dit_fused_fp16.xml` is not present in that directory, omit `--use-fused-dit`, or use the updated `ov_n1d7_forward.py` which can auto-fallback to the 4-component action-head path.
+
+### Notes
+
+- For ALOHA, `--num-cameras` must be `1` or `4`
+- Requires a real dataset in LeRobot format
+
+---
+
+## Output Behavior
+
+During inference the scripts print:
+
+- checkpoint path
+- OpenVINO model directory
+- dataset path (ALOHA) or dummy observation info (base)
+- embodiment adapter name
+- camera configuration
+- selected mode
+- warmup timing
+- per-iteration timing
+- averaged timing breakdown
+
+The timing summary separates:
+
+- ViT
+- LLM prep
+- LLM
+- VL self-attention
+- state encoder
+- fused DiT or 4-component diffusion loop
